@title Dragon Ball - Advanced Adventure (USA)
@file Dragon Ball - Advanced Adventure (U).gba
@game BDVE
@chip EEPROM
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba
@save skip: DATA 1 > Regular > Story writes nothing (the first boot's 61-byte format is all there is; Option holds only Collection and Erase Save Data); the first save is the end of stage 1, past the bridge and its fights, and the frozen fight there parts dingbat from mgba (below)

# Title, DATA 1, Regular, Story, the opening scene, then stage 1 on Mount
# Paozu: walk right punching (B) through the pig soldiers, the locked arena
# by the cliffs (cleared facing left), the downhill fights, to the bridge.
# Findings: the second reference parts at f2571: the pig soldier by the
# bamboo takes a step where dingbat-bios and mgba hold their guard (an AI
# draw); from there it plays its own fight (stage1_start is its last match).
# dingbat-bios and mgba stay on the same frame to past the bridge
# checkpoint, but for single frames every 16 (f3846, f3862, f3878, ...;
# 68 px): the bobbing "!" sign's top three lines (y35-37). The main loop
# starts its tile DMAs to VRAM at 0x0600CE60 at line 37-38 in dingbat
# (0x08008230), after those lines are drawn; mgba's main loop gets there at
# least three lines (~3.7k cycles) sooner. From f9267, in the fights on the
# bridge, dingbat runs a frame behind mgba (one more lag frame) and the
# fight goes differently. Both are the main loop's pricing; mgba's cheaper
# gamepak and EWRAM prices are docs/playtest-bugs.md §63.

